{
  "_README": {
    "purpose": "Declarative bar-shape library for the BBS shape drawer.",
    "how_to_add_a_shape": [
      "Add an entry to the 'shapes' array below.",
      "Coordinates are NORMALISED 0..1 across the drawing canvas:",
      "  x = 0 is left edge, x = 1 is right edge.",
      "  y = 0 is TOP edge,  y = 1 is BOTTOM edge.",
      "A built-in padding maps 0..1 to the usable area.",
      "",
      "Each shape has:",
      "  id        - unique key (used by quick buttons + saved sketches)",
      "  label     - text shown on the quick-shape button",
      "  group     - 'quick' to show as a quick button, or any category name",
      "  segments  - array of polyline segments:",
      "      pts    : [[x,y], ...] normalised points",
      "      style  : 'bend' (arc) | 'straight' (sharp) | 'curve' (spline)",
      "      closed : true to close the loop (optional)",
      "  dims      - dimension lines: {from:[x,y], to:[x,y], label, off:[dx,dy]}",
      "",
      "ISOMETRIC: set iso:true, give points as [x,y,z] world units, set fit.",
      "PARAMETRIC: set generator:'circle' or 'spiral' (turns for spiral).",
      "",
      "NOTE: this file is fetched at runtime; the app must be served over http",
      "(not opened from disk via file://, which browsers block for fetch).",
      "",
      "TIP: Draw a shape in the drawer, click 'Export to shapes.json', paste the",
      "entry into the 'shapes' array here, then reload the app."
    ],
    "schema_version": 2
  },
